{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778976558130,"sessionID":"ses_1ccbc1452ffeszWjsWacrU366B","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_4cC9qVUoWWCPyxt1HHb8HfGu","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json","offset":1,"limit":2000},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"Links #3471 \\n\\nCopilot follow the information below and create new CL for the terms described below:\\n\\n-## Term 1: Intrinsic primary afferent neuron of myenteric plexus\\n\\n**Preferred Label**: intrinsic primary afferent neuron of myenteric plexus\\n\\n**Definition**: A sensory neuron of the enteric nervous system whose soma resides in the myenteric plexus and which functions as the afferent limb of intrinsic reflex circuits controlling motility, secretion, and blood flow. This neuron is characterised by Dogiel type II morphology (large smooth soma with multiple long axon-like processes), AH-type electrophysiology (prolonged afterhyperpolarization following an action potential), and is immunopositive for choline acetyltransferase (ChAT) and immunonegative for neuronal nitric oxide synthase (NOS1).\\n\\n**References**:\\n- PMID:34170401\\n- PMID:37355216\\n- PMID:40954253\\n\\n**UBERON Terms**:\\n- UBERON:0002439 (myenteric nerve plexus) — soma location\\n\\n**Parent CL Terms**:\\n- CL:0007011 (enteric neuron)\\n- CL:0000101 (sensory neuron)\\n\\n**Import Flags**: None\\n\\n**Synonyms**:\\n- IPAN (PMID:34170401)\\n- myenteric sensory neuron (PMID:34170401)\\n- multiaxonal cholinergic myenteric sensory neuron (PMID:37355216)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Term 2: Interneuron of myenteric plexus\\n\\n**Preferred Label**: interneuron of myenteric plexus\\n\\n**Definition**: An interneuron of the enteric nervous system whose soma resides in the myenteric plexus. Interneurons of the myenteric plexus integrate sensory input from intrinsic primary afferent neurons (IPANs) and modulate motor output to smooth muscle and secretory epithelia by synapsing onto motor neurons and other interneurons within the plexus.\\n\\n**References**:\\n- PMID:34170401\\n- PMID:40954253\\n- PMID:32888429\\n\\n**UBERON Terms**:\\n- UBERON:0002439 (myenteric nerve plexus) — soma location\\n\\n**Parent CL Terms**:\\n- CL:0007011 (enteric neuron)\\n- CL:0000099 (interneuron)\\n\\n**Import Flags**: None\\n\\n**Synonyms**:\\n- enteric interneuron ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n3:   \"comments\": [],\n4:   \"title\": \"Links to #3471 Add myenteric neurons for hubmap\",\n5:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3584\"\n6: }\n\n(End of file - total 6 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"Links #3471 \\n\\nCopilot follow the information below and create new CL for the terms described below:\\n\\n-## Term 1: Intrinsic primary afferent neuron of myenteric plexus\\n\\n**Preferred Label**: intrinsic primary afferent neuron of myenteric plexus\\n\\n**Definition**: A sensory neuron of the enteric nervous system whose soma resides in the myenteric plexus and which functions as the afferent limb of intrinsic reflex circuits controlling motility, secretion, and blood flow. This neuron is characterised by Dogiel type II morphology (large smooth soma with multiple long axon-like processes), AH-type electrophysiology (prolonged afterhyperpolarization following an action potential), and is immunopositive for choline acetyltransferase (ChAT) and immunonegative for neuronal nitric oxide synthase (NOS1).\\n\\n**References**:\\n- PMID:34170401\\n- PMID:37355216\\n- PMID:40954253\\n\\n**UBERON Terms**:\\n- UBERON:0002439 (myenteric nerve plexus) — soma location\\n\\n**Parent CL Terms**:\\n- CL:0007011 (enteric neuron)\\n- CL:0000101 (sensory neuron)\\n\\n**Import Flags**: None\\n\\n**Synonyms**:\\n- IPAN (PMID:34170401)\\n- myenteric sensory neuron (PMID:34170401)\\n- multiaxonal cholinergic myenteric sensory neuron (PMID:37355216)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Term 2: Interneuron of myenteric plexus\\n\\n**Preferred Label**: interneuron of myenteric plexus\\n\\n**Definition**: An interneuron of the enteric nervous system whose soma resides in the myenteric plexus. Interneurons of the myenteric plexus integrate sensory input from intrinsic primary afferent neurons (IPANs) and modulate motor output to smooth muscle and secretory epithelia by synapsing onto motor neurons and other interneurons within the plexus.\\n\\n**References**:\\n- PMID:34170401\\n- PMID:40954253\\n- PMID:32888429\\n\\n**UBERON Terms**:\\n- UBERON:0002439 (myenteric nerve plexus) — soma location\\n\\n**Parent CL Terms**:\\n- CL:0007011 (enteric neuron)\\n- CL:0000099 (interneuron)\\n\\n**Import Flags**: None\\n\\n**Synonyms**:\\n- enteric interneuron ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n  \"comments\": [],\n  \"title\": \"Links to #3471 Add myenteric neurons for hubmap\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3584\"\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__issue_context__.json","time":{"start":1778976558080,"end":1778976558128}},"id":"prt_e33440bf8001hUELYJgZQMnQyu","sessionID":"ses_1ccbc1452ffeszWjsWacrU366B","messageID":"msg_e3344015b001VKPi9sR0txV65R"}}
